<td id="A7.T8.2.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">
<span id="A7.T8.2.12.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="A7.T8.2.12.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Where in the human body can you find the Trapezium bone?</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T8.2.12.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">
<span id="A7.T8.2.12.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="A7.T8.2.12.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">The term ‘Trapezium’ is a less commonly known anatomical term.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T8.2.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T8.2.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;"></td>
<td id="A7.T8.2.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">✗</td>
