<span id="A7.T8.2.16.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Superlative Usage</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T8.2.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">✓</td>
<td id="A7.T8.2.16.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">
<span id="A7.T8.2.16.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="A7.T8.2.16.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">What is the first stage of cellular respiration?</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T8.2.16.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">
<span id="A7.T8.2.16.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:156.5pt;">
<span id="A7.T8.2.16.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">The word ‘first’ introduces a superlative comparison.</span>
</span></td></tr>
